"""
Creates a plot that looks at d(x) from data_postBend - data_preBend instead of
|data - linearREF| (as in Analysis_Script_fit_v1.py).
Then, creates a plot of the local twist angle based on the d(x) plot. 

This script uses two methodologies to match the before and after traces. 
The first matches the traces by a fitted curve parameterization of the ribbon edge, 
and samples both traces at the same arclength along the ribbon. 
The second matches the traces by the user-selected corresponding points. 

In order for this script to be compatible with both methods, the before/after coordinate trace files 
should contain the same number of clicked points. 

Both traces are interpolated at the same coordinate along the ribbon, and deflection is calculated as the signed displacement of the post trace along the local normal of the pre trace:
    d(s) = (r_post(s) - r_pre(s)) . n_pre(s)

Align the before and after AFM images before clicking points whenever
possible. Otherwise global scan translation/rotation will be included in d(s).
"""

# ==============================================================================
# region - Imports and path setting
# ==============================================================================

